1|0@DarkNetMarkets^1440798727#cuj4cyh:PirateRadioSignal$:No, you should be fine. After the import, MultiBit then replays the blockchain from the replay date to find the transactions for the new private keys. For blockchain.info wallets the blockchain must be replayed from the first block. This can take up to an hour on a wifi connection (depending on the speed of the computer you connect to). It is best just to leave MultiBit to sync the blockchain on its own. And yes, multibit should have you up and running in "no time"
